 3. `inject-contract.mjs` injects `CDP6-CONTRACT v1` at SubagentStart (as `cdp5-agents/hooks/inject-contract.mjs:21-25`) and binds the one unbound pending spawn of that `agent_type` to the `agent_id` from the hook input (hooks.md:2541 input; KR-10); because step 2 allows at most one unbound pending spawn per role, the binding does not rest on start order (A-18 records the order for concurrent spawns of different roles). For teammates see §3.4 item 2.
-4. At `SubagentHandback` (`check-handback.mjs`, as `cdp5-agents/hooks/check-handback.mjs:46-72` reads `tool_input.message` and `agent_id`): acknowledgement, the `run:`/`task:` line, whose task must equal the bound spawn's task (a mismatch denies), hedges, written-file claims (each `wrote: <path>` line names a file whose mtime is later than the spawn time), PII lines; first failure denies once with the reason. When the contract cannot be verified the handback is denied, not passed (CDP5's branch at `check-handback.mjs:54-61` passes it; CDP6 does not copy that). Refusals at capture time (a busy lock, an unreadable run record or `counters.json`, a malformed `index.jsonl`, a capture file of the same name) also deny once per agent id; a later handback of that agent id that still fails is neither denied nor captured and leaves a `hooks observed` line with decision `none`, so the phase exit finds no capture and fails closed (UC-01 Exit). Only an unverifiable contract and a missing `agent_id` deny every time, also without a data directory; the first ends in STOP-8. A counter-role handback whose capture form (§5.3) fails `verdict-check.mjs` is denied once with the reasons, so the role can restate, also after an earlier deny of the same agent id for another cause, since the marker keeps the capture-form deny apart (SL-2 fix audit F-D); a second failing handback is captured with `validator: rejected`, which the gate does not count as a pass; one that has a verdict (b) or (c) blocks until the owner's record (§5.3 gate decision table) (SL-2 outside review gap 5). A handback whose bound spawn is already closed with a capture of the same message sha256 (the handback call was denied by another hook after the capture) gets no decision and no second capture. Without an absolute `CLAUDE_PLUGIN_DATA` no run is active and nothing is captured, so `check-handback.mjs` gives no decision, as the UC-10 error row says for every hook (SL-2 T2 review, ledger 0021).
